                <p rendition="#center">1. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Letter of Senior Secretary of
                        the Joint Secretariat, Mr. Norman Brook</hi>
                </p>
                <p>The Joint Secretariat are authorised to supply to representatives of the Italian
                    Government, on request, copies of the statements made to the Council by the
                    Yugoslav representatives (C.F.M.(45) 26 and 31<anchor n="17" xml:id="d115-f2"/>)
                    on the question of the Yugoslav-Italian frontier and Trieste.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">2. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Record of Proceedings of the
                        Council</hi>
                </p>
                <p>The daily record prepared by the Joint Secretariat in accordance with C.F.M.(45)
                        12<anchor n="18" xml:id="d115-f3"/> should be confined to a record of
                    decisions reached by the Council and should not include any account of the
                    discussions.</p>
                <p>The preparation of a draft Protocol, to be approved by the Council at the
                    conclusion of the present Conference, should be begun without <pb facs="0300"
                        n="288" xml:id="pg288"/> further delay by a Committee consisting of the
                    Secretaries of the Delegations.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">3. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Roumania: Peace Treaty</hi>
                </p>
                <p>An exchange of views took place between <hi rendition="#small-caps">M.
                        Molotov</hi> and <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Byrnes</hi> about the note
                    of reservation prefixed to the memorandum by the United States Delegation
                    (C.F.M.(45) 36)<anchor n="19" xml:id="d115-f4"/>.</p>
            </div>
